  "details": "Pain-Point:\n\nWorld creators in VRChat have no real authority over who stays in the worlds they've built. If someone joins to harass users or ruin the experience, the creator can report them and wait, most of the time over a day, while the person is still in the world causing problems. Platforms like Roblox have already solved this with creator ban tools, and it works very well.\n\nFeature:\n\ntemporary world bans, capped at 90 days. This would allow creators to moderate their worlds and help prevent against bad users, something like this should be tied to the users IP or HWID since that is already logged by VRChat as to prevent the bad user from using alt accounts at least easily to ban evade as they can do with Instance bans.\n\nConcern:\n\nA world creator could be a bad actor and just ban anyone they want but it would only be temporary and it would only serve to harm their own world.\n\ni do not know how to word any of this any better, the biggest pain-point is that users feel like they can just do whatever and just be able to continue to do it over and over eg. Client users or terminally online trolls and as a creator you can't do anything at all about it unless you want to get a ban on vrc even though that seems really backwards.",
